<!--
    Objective-C categories, protocols and instance layouts (`option objc on|off`,
    `option objcivars on|off`).

    Issue: on an ObjC-heavy iOS app (ios_kcm, 1.9 MB arm64) the `objc` pass left
    every category method a `sub_<addr>` (77 of them: categories extend classes
    that live in other images, so the class walk never reaches their IMPs), every
    ivar access read `*(long *)((long)self + dat_1001aea74)` (505 sites: the
    `__objc_ivar` offset variable had a 1-byte label the 4-byte load never
    matched), and a selector this image only declared in a protocol
    (`UITableViewDelegate`'s 53 methods) typed nothing.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement. `analyzers/objc/kuna_objccats.rs`
    reads `__objc_catlist`/`__objc_nlcatlist` (class off its class_t, or off the
    chained import / classic LC_DYLD_INFO bind name) so the method walk renames
    `-[Class(Category) sel]`; `kuna_objcprotos.rs` reads `__objc_protolist`,
    names each `protocol_t` `_OBJC_PROTOCOL_$_<P>` and records the declared
    encodings for the `objc_msgSend$<sel>` stub prototypes; `kuna_objcivars.rs`
    builds `struct <Class>` from `class_ro_t.ivars` (offset variable values,
    encodings) and types `self`, with the offset variables reported constant
    through the `dynrelocs` fold path (P3) under `objcivars`.

    P0 assertions: `option objc on|off`, `option objcivars on|off` (the latter
    also an env-bridged load-time setting: set BEFORE the `load file` it applies
    to, so pass 2 flips it ahead of its load and pass 3 flips it back).

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; every pass clears it
    and loads the real arm64 fixture through the object bootstrap. The fixture
    is `macho_objc_meta.m`: root class `Base {isa; int count; double ratio; id
    name}`, protocol `Greeter` (`greet:` required, `wave` optional), category
    `Base(Extra) <Greeter>`, category `Remote(Extra)` on an undefined (bind)
    class, and `Sub : Remote {int x; id tag}` whose `-[Sub x]` goes through the
    `__objc_ivar` offset variable; `use` sends `wave` through a linker stub.
    Linked `-fixup_chains -objc_stubs_fast -x` with the `_OBJC_IVAR_$_` symbols
    made local (stripped) as in a shipped app; see the fixtures README.

    Pass 1 (`option objc off`, the shipped default) reproduces the BUG: the
    category method is `sub_10000083c`, `-[Sub x]` reads
    `*(unsigned int *)(a0 + dat_100008388)`, and the stub is `sub_1000008e0()`.
    Pass 2 (`option objc on`, `option objcivars off`) proves the NAMING on its
    own: `-[Base(Extra) greet:]`, `-[Sub x]` with `self` still `objc_object *`
    reading `(int8)self + (int8)Sub::x`, and `objc_msgSend$wave(a0)` typed from
    the protocol's `v16@0:8` (one argument, the receiver).
    Pass 3 (`option objc on`, `objcivars` at its default) is the FIX: `Base
    *self` with `self->ratio` / `self->count`, and `Sub *self` with `self->x`
    through the folded offset variable.
-->
